n\": \"An Ultrasonic Gas Meter (manufacturer's mark: Elster). Q.Sonic^max: 6 direct paths and 2 reflection swirl paths; Q.Sonic^max6: 6 direct paths (identical to Q.Sonic^max with the two swirl paths removed). Destined for the measurement of gas volume. Construction recorded in documentation folder T10586-5.\"\n}\n```\n\nmodule_designation: omit or null. I'll omit.\n\nmodel_family:\n```json\n{\n  \"family_name\": \"Q.Sonic\",\n  \"models\": [ ...29 entries... ]\n}\n```\n\nEach model entry:\n{\"model_id\": \"Q.Sonic^max DN100\", \"label\": \"Q.Sonic^max, 4 in / DN100\", \"attributes\": {\"diameter_size_inch\": 4, \"diameter_size_dn\": 100, \"accuracy_class\": \"0.5; 1.0\", \"direct_path_count\": 6, \"reflection_swirl_path_count\": 2}}\n\nFor max6: accuracy_class \"1.0\", direct 6, swirl 0.\n\nThat's 29 entries — write them all.\n\nLabels: \"4 inch\" or \"4 in\"? Use \"4 in\".\n\nrecommendation:\n{\"id\": \"R137-1\", \"edition\": 2012, \"scheme\": \"A\", \"accuracy_classes\": [\"0.5\", \"1.0\"]}\n\ntest_reports as above.\n\nrevision_history:\n[\n  {\"revision\": \"Initial\", \"date\": \"2020-11-02\", \"changes\": null},\n  {\"revision\": \"1\", \"date\": \"2021-08-26\", \"changes\": \"Revision due to new hardware: Field terminal board version BD; Main Board version AJ.\"},\n  {\"revision\": \"2\", \"date\": \"2022-08-18\", \"changes\": \"Addition of firmware V3.40.\"},\n  {\"revision\": \"3\", \"date\": \"2022-12-13\", \"changes\": \"New Board (Ethernet Range Extender).\"},\n  {\"revision\": \"4\", \"date\": \"2025-06-11\", \"changes\": \"Addition of Q.Sonic^max6 6-path meters for accuracy Class 1.0 only.\"}\n]\n\nfootnotes:\n[\n  {\"marker\": \"1)\", \"text\": \"Basically the Q.Sonic^max6 is identical to the Q.Sonic^max with the two swirl paths removed. (Page 2, path configuration)\"},\n  {\"marker\": \"1)\", \"text\": \"If higher values are chosen for Qmin and/or Qt and/or lower values for Qmax, it has to be taken into account that: 5 ≤ Qmax/Qmin < 50: Qmax/Qt ≥ 5; Qmax/Qmin ≥ 50: Qmax/Qt ≥ 10. (Tables 3 and 4)\"},\n  {\"marker\": \"★)\", \"text\": \"These software modules are only mandatory if volume conversion is performed by the instrument. If this is not the case, the software modules are optional.\"}\n]\n\nHmm the parenthetical context additions — helpful disambiguation; slight addition but not fabrication. OK.\n\nmatrix_tables: 3 tables (software, table 3, table 4).\n\nLet me write table 3 rows:\n{\"diameter_size_inch\": 4, \"diameter_size_dn\": 100, \"minimum_internal_bore\": 90, \"maximum_internal_bore\": 102.3, \"minimum_flow_velocity\": 0.49, \"transitional_flow_velocity\": 2.3, \"maximum_flow_velocity\": 37.6}\n... etc.\n\nColumns naming: [\"diameter_size_inch\", \"diameter_size_dn\", \"minimum_internal_bore_id_min\", \"maximum_internal_bore_id_max\", \"minimum_flow_velocity_v_min\", \"transitional_flow_velocity_v_t\", \"maximum_flow_velocity_v_max\"]. Keep consistent with model_level attribute names. Let me use attribute names: \"minimum_internal_bore\", \"maximum_internal_bore\", \"minimum_flow_velocity\", \"transitional_flow_velocity\", \"maximum_flow_velocity\". And models[].attributes dn/inch.\n\nFor model_level attributes, I'll use: \"minimum_internal_bore\" (mm), \"maximum_internal_bore\" (mm), \"minimum_flow_velocity\" (m/s), \"transitional_flow_velocity\" (m/s), \"maximum_flow_velocity\" (m/s). Drop the Vmin/IDmin suffixes? Rule 1 examples keep symbols sometimes (nlc, plc). I'll name them with subscript context: \"minimum_flow_velocity_vmin\"? Hmm rule examples: \"ratio_y_emax_over_vmin\". I'll use: \"minimum_internal_bore_id_min\" → maybe simpler: \"internal_bore_min_idmin\"? Overthinking. Use \"minimum_internal_bore\", \"maximum_internal_bore\", \"minimum_flow_velocity\", \"transitional_flow_velocity\", \"maximum_flow_velocity\". Clean and unambiguous.\n\nAlso dn attribute in models: \"diameter_size_dn\". OK.\n\nFor v_t values in table 3 — footnote_markers [\"1)\",\"2)\"] per value. In matrix tables, note