 of the Q.Sonic^max6 family of instruments\" spanning pages 4-5.\n\nMatrix table descriptions:\n- Table 3: \"Q = V · 1/4 · π · ID² · 3600 = 900 · π · ID² · V, where Q = flow rate [m³/h], V = velocity [m/s], ID = inner diameter [m].\"\n- Table 4 same description.\n\nAlso models list — I'll write attributes as {\"dn\": ..., \"inch\": ..., \"accuracy_class\": ..., \"direct_path_count\": 6, \"reflection_swirl_path_count\": ...}. Use short keys \"dn\", \"inch\" or \"diameter_size_dn\"? Consistent with matrix columns: \"diameter_size_inch\", \"diameter_size_dn\". Use those.\n\nWriting now. Given size, be systematic.\n\nmodels array:\n\n1. {\"model_id\": \"Q.Sonic^max DN100\", \"label\": \"Q.Sonic^max, 4 in / DN100\", \"attributes\": {\"diameter_size_inch\": 4, \"diameter_size_dn\": 100, \"accuracy_class\": \"0.5; 1.0\", \"direct_path_count\": 6, \"reflection_swirl_path_count\": 2}}\n2. DN150 (6), 3. DN200 (8), 4. DN250 (10), 5. DN300 (12), 6. DN350 (14), 7. DN400 (16), 8. DN450 (18), 9. DN500 (20), 10. DN550 (22), 11. DN600 (24), 12. DN650 (26), 13. DN750 (30), 14. DN900 (36)\n15. {\"model_id\": \"Q.Sonic^max6 DN80\", \"label\": \"Q.Sonic^max6, 3 in / DN80\", \"attributes\": {..., accuracy_class: \"1.0\", direct 6, swirl 0}}\n16. DN100 (4), 17. DN150 (6), 18. DN200 (8), 19. DN250 (10), 20. DN300 (12), 21. DN350 (14), 22. DN400 (16), 23. DN450 (18), 24. DN500 (20), 25. DN550 (22), 26. DN600 (24), 27. DN650 (26), 28. DN750 (30), 29. DN900 (36)\n\nTo trim, attributes per max model are identical objects except dn/inch — fine, repeat.\n\nActually, hmm — could shorten attributes per model to just {\"diameter_size_inch\", \"diameter_size_dn\"} and add two pseudo-model-level or keep accuracy/path in a separate place... No, keep as planned; explicitness is good.\n\nmodel_level entries — write values arrays fully.\n\nminimum_internal_bore (mm):\n[\n{\"model\":\"Q.Sonic^max DN100\",\"value\":90},\n{\"model\":\"Q.Sonic^max DN150\",\"value\":139},\n{\"model\":\"Q.Sonic^max DN200\",\"v