perating_pressure_ratio attribute still valuable. OK.\n\"minimum_outlet_straight_pipe_length\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 3, \"max\": null}, \"unit_symbol\": \"D\", \"unit_id\": null}\n\"temperature_sensor_distance_from_meter_outlet\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 2, \"max\": 5}, \"unit_symbol\": \"D\", \"unit_id\": null}\n\"inlet_pipe_diameter_tolerance\": {\"value\": 3, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\", \"unit_id\": null}\n\"flow_direction\": {\"value\": \"bi-directional\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null}\n\"bidirectional_conformity_verification\": {\"value\": \"verification in one direction is sufficient\", ...} — maybe merge into flow_direction note. I'll keep flow_direction only.\n\nDrop humidity_condition? Table says \"M1 / E2 Condensing humidity\". Keep.\n\nNow finalize. Also double-check \"18 – 30 V DC\": voltage 18–30 V, type DC. ✓.\n\nI think we're ready. Write the entire JSON compactly but readable. Ensure no trailing commas.",
